<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n29303" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mĭsy</span></b> , yos (in
		the <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>gen.</i> also
			misys, <i><span class="en">Scrib. Comp. 34</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">and, misy,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cels.
					6, 7, 2</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">5, 19, 15</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Veg. 6, 16, 1</span></i>), n.,
			= <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μίσυ</span>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A kind of mushroom</i> or <i>truffle</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 19, 3, 12, §
			36</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A mineral</i>, perh. <i>a vitriolic
				ore, copperas, sory</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 34,
				12, 27, § 114</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Cels. 5,
				19, 8</span></i>; <i><span class="en">27</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Scrib. Comp. 34</span></i>; <i><span class="en">240</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
